  "verbalization": "Cabergoline, a dopamine receptor agonist, is linked to SNB-78 through a series of molecular interactions that involve the enzyme 5alpha,6alpha-Epoxy(22e,24r)-ergosta-8(14),22-dien-3beta,7alpha-diol and 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One. These compounds are all targets of cabergoline, suggesting a potential mechanism of action where the drug influences the activity of these enzymes. The evidence indicates that cabergoline may modulate the expression or function of these targets, which in turn affect SNB-78. The presence of multiple pathways connecting cabergoline to SNB-78 highlights a possible role in regulating downstream molecular processes, possibly through enzyme inhibition or activation. The integration of these pathways suggests that cabergoline may exert its effects by influencing the activity of these enzymes, which could be a key mechanism underlying its interaction with SNB-78.",
